This module defines a hierarchical set of `[ftxui::Element](namespaceftxui.html#a2bc31f2d685189e5c61d2293a1f51b4f)`. An element manages the layout and can be responsive to the terminal dimension changes. Note the following example where this module is used to create a simple layout with a number of operators:

The [Example](module-dom-examples.html) section provides a collection of examples.

**Example:**

namespace [ftxui](namespaceftxui.html) {

...

// Define the document

Element document = [vbox](group__dom.html#gafd28058f0ccbbdf34691a85a7cc9b2e3)({

[text](group__dom.html#ga0564a46b4e72126a61c6f19cd5de8d46)("The window") | bold | [color](group__dom.html#gadef6e6e66199153de6d3b21b14dcf868)(Color::Blue),

[gauge](group__dom.html#gae0b8041a60629fd790716038738c93ce)(0.5)

text("The footer")

});

// Add a border, by calling the \`ftxui::border\` decorator function.

document = border(document);

// Add another border, using the pipe operator.

document = document | border.

// Add another border, using the |= operator.

document |= border

...

}

